{
  "id": "30367_machikireru",
  "headword": "{待|ま}ちきれる",
  "reading": "まちきれる",
  "romaji": "machikireru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to be able to wait (usu. negative: can't wait)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be able to wait; (in the negative) to not be able to wait",
      "explanation": "To be capable of waiting until something finally arrives. Used almost exclusively in the negative {待|ま}ちきれない, which expresses impatient excitement — \"I can't wait.\""
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30367_machikireru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{明日|あした}が{待|ま}ちきれない。",
      "english": "I can't wait for tomorrow.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30367_machikireru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもたちは{夏休|なつやす}みが{待|ま}ちきれない{様子|ようす}だ。",
      "english": "The children look like they can't wait for summer vacation.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30367_machikireru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{結果|けっか}の{発表|はっぴょう}を{待|ま}ちきれずに、{先生|せんせい}に{直接|ちょくせつ}{聞|き}きに{行|い}った。",
      "english": "Unable to wait for the results to be announced, I went to ask the teacher directly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30367_machikireru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しいゲームの{発売日|はつばいび}まであと{一週間|いっしゅうかん}もあるなんて、とても{待|ま}ちきれない。",
      "english": "A whole week left until the new game comes out — I really can't wait.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The potential form of {待|ま}ちきる ({待|ま}つ \"wait\" + 〜きる \"do completely\"). The affirmative is rare; learners will meet this word as {待|ま}ちきれない or the adverbial {待|ま}ちきれず(に).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ...が{待|ま}ちきれない: can't wait for ...\n- {待|ま}ちきれずに〜する: to do something without waiting any longer\n- {待|ま}ちきれない{様子|ようす}: looking unable to wait\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {楽|たの}しみにする: to look forward to — states anticipation calmly, without the sense of straining at the delay\n- {待|ま}ち{遠|どお}しい: eagerly awaited — an adjective describing the awaited thing, not the person waiting",
